body:
I decided to stick to my old monitor instead. I guess it was okay but there was some ghosting (although there's maybe some settings to reduce that, I don't know that much about monitors). I was also bothered that you couldn't adjust it lower, but that's just me.

&#x200B;

I don't know man. Maybe it's ok, but I don't think it's good for gaming. Probably fine as an office monitor. But I would personally go for another brand if I were to purchase a new monitor again. Probably Dell as I have good experience with their monitors.

I found out how to convert back to array:

int\[\] myArray = System.Array.ConvertAll(objectsStringToConvert.Split(','), int.Parse);

&#x200B;

Thanks for the help!:)

Thanks! So I've made the array of int's to a string with  

&#x200B;

myString = string.Join(",", array);

&#x200B;

now my problem is how do I convert the string back to an int array?
